<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">content-visibility: auto skips rendering off-screen sections, but without contain-intrinsic-size those sections collapse to near-zero height and cause scroll jank.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Pair it with contain-intrinsic-size: auto &lt;fallback&gt; — the fallback covers the first render, the auto keyword remembers the real size after that.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Size the fallback from real measured data per section type, and explicitly test sticky/fixed descendants and CLS impact before shipping the change.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
